-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner unit and the level-N Hecke criterion
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N,q,q'$ with $N$ nonzero, $q$ and $q'$ prime, $q\nmid N$, $q'\nmid N$ and $q'\neq q$, and rationals $a,b$ such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completed algebra $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $v$ contains $q$ or $q'$. Let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order (a finitely generated $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication, $\mathbb{Q}$-spanning $B$, and maximal among such), let $N$ be squarefree, let $R\le\Lambda$ be an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. an intersection of two maximal orders having relative index $N$ in the first, let $\iota:B\to M_2(\mathbb{R})$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map, and let $J'$ satisfy $\Lambda\le J'$, $\Lambda J'\subseteq J'$, $N J'\subseteq\Lambda$, relative index of $\Lambda$ in $J'$ equal to $N^2$, and, for $x\in\Lambda$, $x\in R$ iff $J'x\subseteq J'$. Then there are a unit $w_N\in B^{\times}$ and $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ with $g=\iota(w_N)$ and $\det g>0$ such that: $x\in R\iff w_Nxw_N^{-1}\in R$ for all $x$; conjugation by $w_N$ preserves `nrd`; $\gamma\in$ `fuchsianGroup R ι` iff $g\gamma g^{-1}\in$ `fuchsianGroup R ι` (the group being the image under $\iota$ of the subgroup generated by the units of $R$, intersected with the determinant-one kernel); every $u$ that is a unit of $R$ with inverse in $R$ and $\mathrm{nrd}(u)=1$ equals the matrix of some element of that group; and for every prime $\ell\neq q,q'$, every $\tau$ in the upper half-plane and every $t\in R$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(t)=\ell$, the identity $\ell\,L_\tau(J')+L_\tau(\Lambda t)=L_\tau(J't)$ in $\mathbb{C}^2$, where $L_\tau(X)=\{\iota(x)\binom{\tau}{1}:x\in X\}$ via `qmPeriodMap`/`qmPeriodLattice`, holds if and only if $(w_Ntw_N^{-1})\otimes 1$ in $B\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}$ (finite adeles) is the image of some element of `levelHeckeUSet Λ R ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$, and of `primeHeckeSet R ℓ` otherwise.
--
--   This packages the Atkin–Lehner involution $w_N$ of an Eichler order of squarefree level $N$ in an indefinite rational quaternion algebra together with the translation, under conjugation by $w_N$, of the 'level identity' on period lattices at a point $\tau$ into membership in the idelic Hecke set used by the Čerednik–Drinfeld model. It is used in the construction of period maps for meromorphic realisations on uniformised Hecke curves.
